968 bytes is a full string-/depth-aware walker + one slice, not a stub.

Sole product call site (`.oo` + ELF): `c_secret_emit_guard` sys_exec branch —
`let last: String = c_sys_exec_last_arg(args)` then cap-ident refuse.

### Emit-time declaration order — PASS

`.oo` order: `c_sys_exec_last_arg` defined in `c_emit_args.oo`; callee in
`c_emit_secret_guard.oo`. Product `cli_emit.oo` default `emit-c` is
`protos` then `bodies`. Live emit of the args module printed, before any `{`:

```
OoStr c_sys_exec_last_arg(OoStr args);
```

then later `OoStr c_sys_exec_last_arg(OoStr args) { ... }`.

`c_emit_ty.oo` / `c_emit_let_ext.oo` list `c_sys_exec_last_arg` as **OoStr** —
this is why **this** helper re-emits on the current host (7.1 walker did not:
untyped `let is_start` → `unknown free call oo_str_eq`).

