========================================================================
2. `oo_str_slice` not concat; no leftover `char[N]`
========================================================================

### Source (.oo) — PASS

`c_sys_exec_last_arg` (`ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo` L71–131 after honesty comment):

- Scanner: string-/escape-/depth-aware top-level commas; records `last_start`.
- Extract: `let out = str_slice(args, last_start, n);`
- **No** `out = out + char_at`.
- **No** `char buf[N]` (language has no stack `char[]` in `.oo`).

SPRINT “stack buffer” wording = do not cap the last arg in a fixed C array
**and** do not rebuild it char-by-char. Alpha close = **one slice for the span**
(`t1_memory.oot` M-SG3).

### Product machine code — PASS

`objdump` of `c_sys_exec_last_arg` (968 B):

| Callee | Count | Role |
|--------|------:|------|
| `oo_str_lit` | 9 | `"\\"` / `"\""` / `"("` / `")"` / `","` / `" "` / empty / empty-args snippet |
| `oo_str_eq` | 8 | same classification |
| `oo_str_release` | 5 | stored `OoStr` temps |
| `oo_str_retain` | 2 | return `args` / `out` |
| `oo_char_at` | 3 | walk + space skip |
| `oo_chars_len` | 1 | `n` |
| `oo_str_slice` | **1** | **the last-arg span** |
| `oo_str_concat` | **0** | — |

- **Zero** `sprintf` / `strncpy` / `strcpy` / `strcat` / `memcpy` / `malloc`.
- Entry: `sub $0x68, %rsp` — 104-byte spill frame for `OoStr` pair + callee-saves,
  **not** a `char last[N]`.
- `char` text in the dump is only `oo_char_at` / `oo_chars_len` names.

Live `emit-c` body (exit 0) matches:

```
OoStr out = oo_str_slice(args, last_start, n);
```

No `oo_str_concat` / `char[` inside that function. (Module-level concat at
`c_args_strip_cr` `out = out + c` is **other OWN**, not 7.2.)

Adjacent `c_args_drop_first`: also `oo_str_slice`×1, **0** concat (bonus; not SPRINT 7.2).

### Seed ELF contrast — honesty (not the product host)

`ooda/bootstrap/seed/oodac` (`878392` B, 2026-08-11):

| Probe | Result |
|-------|--------|
| `nm -S` | `000000000044df30 00000000000003b1 T c_sys_exec_last_arg` |
| `oo_str_concat` in that fn | **1** |
| `oo_str_slice` in that fn | **0** |

Seed is the **old** per-char / concat last-arg. Product host at
`ooda/oodac/oodac` is the **fixed** ELF. 7.2 proof is the latter.

### Floor (chs_rt, not primary) — note only

`runtime/chs_rt_str.c`:

- `oo_char_at` — heap 1-char (or UTF-8 1–4 byte) `OoStr` via `oo_str_alloc_payload`.
- `oo_str_slice` — heap copy of the `[start,end)` UTF-8 span (O(|span|)), fail-soft empty on OOB.

These are the **runtime** implementations the emitted walk calls. There is
**no** `c_sys_exec_last_arg` in `chs_rt*.c` / `chs_rt.h`.

### Unreclaimed temps (residual, not 7.2 CRIT)

Space-skip uses **inline** `char_at(args, j)` inside `oo_str_eq(...)` (emit L265).
Stored loop `c` is `oo_str_release`d. Inline results are not. O(n) 1-char leak
on whitespace after commas — not a stack overflow and not last-arg concat.

