4. chs_rt `sys_exec` not primary (no emit ABI break)
========================================================================

| Surface | `c_sys_exec_last_arg` | `oo_sys_exec` |
|---------|----------------------|---------------|
| `ooda/runtime/chs_rt*.c` / `.h` | **absent** | **definition** (`chs_rt_sys.c` L224; proto `chs_rt.h` L252) |
| `ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo` | **definition** | not here |
| `ooda/oodac/c_emit_lower.oo` | not here | emit: `oo_sys_exec(a0, (int)(sizeof((OoStr[]){rest})/sizeof(OoStr)), (OoStr[]){rest})` |
| `ooda/oodac/c_emit_preamble.oo` | n/a | `OoResS oo_sys_exec(long long,int,OoStr*);` |
| Product `oodac` ELF | **T** (compiler) | **T** (linked floor, 725 B) |

`oo_sys_exec` is fork + `execvp` + DE1.8 env filter. `oo_sys_exec1` is
`sh -c` argv wrapper. **Different job, different ABI** (`OoResS`, cap + argc + argv).

Last-arg is **emit-time C-text** extract for SECRET refuse of the last top-level
arg. It does **not** change how product `sys_exec` is lowered. Because emit ABI
is unchanged, this auditor does **not** treat `chs_rt_sys.c` as a second
implementation of 7.2 and does **not** require a runtime-sys_exec re-home.

